{"parentUuid": "243fc212-65c3-5dd6-aa93-ee30f4bea6c6", "isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/work/linkshelf", "sessionId": "524c85c8-b00d-559d-a0ed-d3746faa219d", "version": "2.1.30", "gitBranch": "main", "type": "assistant", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Confirmed: the JSON store is read-modify-write with no locking, so two concurrent `add` calls interleave their writes and corrupt the file. A lock file would patch it, but I'd rather move to SQLite, which handles concurrent writers."}]}, "uuid": "b1e588a9-631b-5a6e-9d54-710462f1a9e4", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T08:32:28.000Z"}
